llama: one recurrent snapshot group for a prompt ubatch

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus the patches before this one in patches/series. This patch
needs patches/hexagon-spec/0002 before it, which gives the rollback its checked limit.

Files:
    src/llama-cparams.h             llama_n_rs_groups(), the shared rule
    src/llama-context.cpp           the per-ubatch value in the copy that the graph gets
    src/llama-graph.h               the value in the reuse key of the graph
    src/llama-memory-recurrent.cpp  the same rule for the depth of the rollback

The problem

Speculation costs the prefill 2.1 times. Measured on the phone, 4B Q8_0, pp512, thermal 0, off
the charger: 899.65 t/s with the switch off and 425.08 t/s with it on, on one build. A shell
llama-bench of the same libraries gives 911.84 t/s.

The switch gives the context n_rs_seq = 3, thus K = 4 (llama_jni.cpp sets cp.n_rs_seq to
kSpecDraftMax). K reaches the prefill graph through cparams.n_rs_seq, and it stops two kernels
of a batch:

  1. The HMX chunked delta rule refuses. gdn-chunk-ops.c:1094 reads
     "if (K != 1) refuse = the op keeps more than the final state". The op then runs
     gated_delta_net_f32_pp_thread, which carries the whole cliff. GATED_DELTA_NET costs 78 ms of
     a 512 token prefill on the chunked path.
  2. The fused conv chunk refuses. build_conv_state emits K copy nodes of the CONCAT, and
     htp-gdn-match.h:327 reads "more than one CPY of the CONCAT on a batch (rollback snapshots)".
     Thus GDN_CONV_CHUNK is never emitted while speculation is on, and the conv work of
     patches/hexagon-kernels is dead on that path. This is a second, independent cause.

Neither refusal is a defect of the kernels. The prefill asks for four rollback groups that no
caller reads.

The rule

A verify step of speculative decoding submits one token for each drafted token, plus the token
of the step before it. common_params_speculative::need_n_rs_seq() sets n_rs_seq to the largest
draft, thus a verify step never holds more than n_rs_seq + 1 tokens of one sequence. A ubatch
that holds more tokens of one sequence is a prompt, and no rollback reaches into it. Such a
ubatch writes one group.

llama_n_rs_groups(n_rs_seq, n_seq_tokens) in llama-cparams.h holds the rule.
llama_context::graph_params writes the value into the cparams copy that the graph gets, thus one
line reaches every model builder and the conv path and the state path of each one cannot
disagree. The context member keeps the count of the whole memory, thus llama_n_rs_seq(), the
size of the cache and the ubatch split do not change.

Two properties make the rule safe:

  - It depends on the shape of the ubatch only. llm_graph_params::allow_reuse compares
    n_seq_tokens, thus a graph that comes from the cache always carries the value of its own
    ubatch. The patch adds n_rs_seq to that comparison as well, because a later rule that is not
    a function of the shape would otherwise reuse a graph of a different topology with no error
    message.
  - llama_memory_recurrent::set_rs_depth calls the same function. Thus a rollback that reaches a
    group which the ubatch did not write makes llama_memory_seq_rm return false, and the caller
    replays the tokens or restores a checkpoint. Patch 0001 gives that limit.

The measurement

A host program counts the nodes of the graph through the eval callback of the scheduler. The
model is Qwen3.5-2B Q4_0 on the CPU backend, 18 linear layers.

    n_rs_seq   ubatch tokens   K       GATED_DELTA_NET output rows   CPY nodes
    0          64              1       192                           72
    3          64              4 -> 1  576 -> 192                    126 -> 72
    3          4               4       516                           126
    3          1               4       513                           126
    8          64              9 -> 1  1216 -> 192                   216 -> 72
    8          4               9       1156                          216
    8          1               9       1153                          216

The prefill graph of a context with rollback groups is now the graph of a context without them,
node for node. A verify step of 4 tokens and a decode of 1 token keep every group.

The logits of a prefill of 64 tokens agree bitwise between n_rs_seq 0 and n_rs_seq 3, before the
patch and after it.

What this changes for a caller

A partial llama_memory_seq_rm right after a prompt ubatch of more than K tokens now returns
false. Before the patch it gave a correct state for a rollback of 1 to n_rs_seq tokens. No caller
in the tree does this: the speculative loop of tools/server and the spec_step of the app both
roll back inside the verify ubatch, which keeps its groups.

State of the verification

The host program above ran on the CPU backend with the 2B Q4_0 file. The Android build of the
pinned container compiles the change. The device has not run it: the prefill number of the phone
is the measurement that stays open.
